    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Frame objects: Evaluation is a declared question with known result family, evidence basis, decision authority and material-operation authority where needed, admitting judgment, prediction, construction, comparison, proof, refusal, classification or action recommendation. Evaluation family shares required manifold, authority basis and result algebra. Workspace is bounded reasoned-over or acted-on material, potentially broader than a repository. Material-relation manifold is the finite jointly interpretable variables, entities, identities, states, relations, invariants, authorities, observations and exclusions needed by a family, allowing overlapping coordinate charts without implied geometry or runtime. Coordinate is complete locally required basis, identity, lineage, input, evidence and authority information. Topology is the material relation structure visible at one basis, not necessarily complete workspace topology. Capability envelope is required competence, context capacity, tools, access, independence and configuration. Reference frame specifies finite attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations for a family and basis. Activated frame binds declaration to exact evaluation, workspace subject, basis, actor and evidence-acquisition boundary. Frame set is a human-declared available family permitting overlaps, alternatives, specialists, exploration and separate assurance. Active frame configuration is activations and declared result relations for one evaluation or decision. Lens is a reusable question family, becoming a frame only on full bounded instantiation. Role allocates responsibility/authority; persona changes approach/salience; abstraction hides/contracts detail; component is structural. None is a frame merely by identity.",
