    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "P0 Bounded construction is recovered: finite actors realise selected outer contracts through fitting steps, owning their internal path; actors may change and reacquire declared sources but not private memory, step-produced facts are not reacquirable, the world is open and output is candidate until evaluated. P1 Interpretation is independent: subject, representation and context-bound meaning differ; structural success is not fidelity and semantic decisions require exact contracts. P2 Purpose is independent: selected outcome defines adequacy and interface obligations derive from the served transformation. P3 Identity is independent: declared authority/kind/value identity survives admissible change and boundaries carry proof obligations. P4a Typed composition is independent: prior type and judgment must satisfy the next exact domain and preconditions, retaining identities, intermediate results, judgments, evidence, authority, provenance and stop states. P4b Conservation is derived from P0 and P2 plus non-reacquirability: producing steps record outer-contract-needed judgments, residuals, observations and authority decisions; reacquirable sources follow sufficiency rather than conservation. P5 Totality is derived from P0 and P6 plus open-world premise: no success on outside-context conditions, first-class non-success and named next moves. P6 Justification and authority is independent: definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports basis-bound claims and authority permits or disposes only within scope.",
